So I did some research and now I see what you attempted to fix. 

So first of all, the changes in Polyflow like this should ALWAYS be accompanied by the test. We can't afford making random fixes like this and hope for the best.

Secondly, as I assumed above, this fix is masking a real bug that is in the constructor of `ExecutionResult`, which should look like this:
```java
    public ExecutionResult(NodeStatus newStatus) {
      this.newStatus = newStatus;
      var nodeProto = AbstractNode.this.protoRef.get();
      this.newOutput = nodeProto.hasNodeOutput() ? nodeProto.getNodeOutput() : null;
    }
```

Please make this change and also add a test that verifies that AbstractNode doesn't set an empty `Any` on failure.
